WEBVTT

00:09:29.055 --> 00:09:31.745
66 -- turn to the calendar with 1966.

00:09:31.769 --> 00:09:33.293
And what month?

00:09:33.317 --> 00:09:34.952
Audience: April.
AB: April what?

00:09:34.976 --> 00:09:35.997
Audience: 17th.

00:09:36.021 --> 00:09:38.325
I believe that was a Sunday.

00:09:38.349 --> 00:09:39.754
Can you confirm, Chris?

00:09:40.883 --> 00:09:41.933
Chris Anderson: Yes.

00:09:41.957 --> 00:09:43.475
AB: I'll tell you what, Chris:

00:09:43.499 --> 00:09:45.688
as long as you have
that book in front of you,

00:09:45.712 --> 00:09:48.976
do me a favor, turn to a year
outside of the 1900s,

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.837
either into the 1800s
or way into the 2000s --

00:09:51.861 --> 00:09:53.893
that'll be a much greater
challenge for me.

00:09:53.917 --> 00:09:55.976
AB: What year would you like?
CA: 1824.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:59.205
AB: 1824, OK.

00:09:59.229 --> 00:10:00.666
AB: And what month?